# Captured FZLP/1 session (benign, verbatim). Lines prefixed ">" are
# client->server, lines prefixed "<" are server->client. Nothing is exploited
# here -- this is a normal provisioning poke, provided so you can see the
# framing exactly as the server produced it.

< FZLP/1 ready
> PING
< PONG
> HELP
< verbs: PING STAT CFG HELP SU
> STAT
< STAT ch0=00 ch1=00 ch2=00 mask=0x00 reserved_admin_ch=0x07
> CFG 1
> 01
> STAT
< OK mask=0x01
> PING
< PONG
> DUMP
< ERR locked: maintenance channel not armed
> SU root
< ERR: SU disabled on this build; channels are provisioned via CFG
> PING
< PONG

